      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(x+1)(x+5).$",
      "worked_solution": "From the equation $y=(x+1)(x+5),$ we can tell that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=-5.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)+(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-3.$",
